<section class="dash-section" aria-labelledby="races-2026-heading">
  <h2 id="races-2026-heading">The 20 races already classified in 2026</h2>
  <table class="dash-table">
    <caption>2026 pole and winner, from each qualifying classification and race classification.</caption>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Round</th>
        <th scope="col">Race</th>
        <th scope="col">Date</th>
        <th scope="col">Pole</th>
        <th scope="col">Winner</th>
        <th scope="col">Pole won</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for race in records.races %}{% if race.season == 2026 %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ race.round }}</td>
        <th scope="row">{{ race.race }}</th>
        <td><time datetime="{{ race.date }}">{{ race.date | displayDate }}</time></td>
        <td><a href="{{ race.qualifyingUrl }}">{{ race.pole }}</a></td>
        <td><a href="{{ race.raceUrl }}">{{ race.winner }}</a></td>
        <td>{% if race.pole == race.winner %}Yes{% else %}No{% endif %}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Austin is round 18 on that list. Antonelli took pole and the race, which is in the <a href="{{ '/articles/2026-10-27-antonelli-wins-austin/' | url }}">United States Grand Prix report</a>. The <a href="{{ '/hubs/austin/' | url }}">Austin hub</a>, the <a href="{{ '/hubs/miami/' | url }}">Miami hub</a> and the <a href="{{ '/hubs/las-vegas/' | url }}">Las Vegas hub</a> collect the US weekend stories. Las Vegas qualifying is already published. The race was not on the results table on 21 November.</p>
</section>

<section class="dash-section" aria-labelledby="circuits-heading">
  <h2 id="circuits-heading">US circuit records</h2>
  <p>Length, laps, distance and the lap record are the figures on the Formula 1 circuit guide and on the matching race page, both opened on 21 November 2026. Turn counts are the ones the circuit guide prints. The year on a lap record is the year Formula 1 prints. It is not a day this desk timed.</p>
  <table class="dash-table">
    <caption>United States circuits on the 2026 Formula 1 calendar.</caption>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Circuit</th>
        <th scope="col">Length</th>
        <th scope="col">Turns</th>
        <th scope="col">Laps</th>
        <th scope="col">Race distance</th>
        <th scope="col">Lap record</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for circuit in records.circuits %}
      <tr>
        <th scope="row"><a href="{{ circuit.hub | url }}">{{ circuit.circuit }}</a></th>
        <td>{{ circuit.lengthKm }} km</td>
        <td>{{ circuit.turns }}</td>
        <td>{{ circuit.laps }}</td>
        <td>{{ circuit.distanceKm }} km</td>
        <td>{{ circuit.lapRecord }} {{ circuit.driver }} ({{ circuit.year }})</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Las Vegas is also on an <a href="https://www.fia.com/sites/default/files/2025_22_usa_f1_r0_timing_racefastestlaps_v01.pdf">FIA fastest laps sheet</a> for the 2025 race: Max Verstappen, 1:33.365, lap 50. That sheet was opened on 21 November 2026. The circuit guide of 19 November 2026 and the <a href="https://www.formula1.com/en/racing/2026/las-vegas">Las Vegas race page</a> print the same time, a length of 6.201 km, 17 turns, 50 laps and 309.958 km. The race page's about text rounds the length to 6.2 km. The table uses 6.201.</p>
  <p>Miami's guide is dated 30 April 2026. It and the <a href="https://www.formula1.com/en/racing/2026/miami">Miami race page</a> print 5.412 km, 57 laps, 308.326 km, and a lap record of 1:29.708 by Max Verstappen in 2023. The guide is the page that says 19 turns. Austin's guide is dated 22 October 2026. It, the <a href="https://www.formula1.com/en/racing/2026/united-states">United States race page</a> and a Formula 1 facts note from the same morning print 5.513 km and a lap record of 1:36.169 by Charles Leclerc in 2019. The guide and the race page also print 56 laps and 308.432 km. The guide is the page that says 20 turns. Start times for the next US race are in the <a href="{{ '/articles/2026-10-27-las-vegas-gp-2026-times/' | url }}">Las Vegas times guide</a>.</p>
</section>

